# the registry of formats
#
# every format mink knows is one registration, listed here on one line, the
# only list of formats. the registry builds once the readers index the link
# phases sniff inputs through and the relocation rows of every pair, and
# refuses a registration whose pairs do not hold: a pair whose code or
# relocation rows are not its own, two pairs of one architecture, or a code
# template no relocation row of its pair patches. it is the route a dependent
# reads files, writes models and looks relocations and trait encodings up
# through, so no dependent names a format's own modules.

